invariant: INV-16
file: p256_ecdh.c
catches: widemul_runtime_test
reason: the scalar multiplication of the key exchange runs under
  WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED whatever answer the exchange was handed, so a session
  whose caller states the multiply runs p256_point_mul on the
  decomposition between a point decode and an affine conversion on the
  wide field. The shared secret is the same, because the two files hold
  the same numbers in a p256_point. bin/widemul_runtime_test requires the
  P-256 operations to call the wide files alone under the constant-time
  answer.

--- old
    widemul_p256_point_mul(widemul, &product, &k, &peer);
--- new
    widemul_p256_point_mul(WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED, &product, &k, &peer);
